{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "האומן", :translit "ha'oman", :gloss "the artisan (i.e., God)"} {:he "תגין על הה\"א", :translit "tagin al ha-heh", :gloss "crowns on the heh"} {:he "בחמשה דברים אב זוכה לבניו", :translit "be-chamisha devarim av zokeiach le-vanav", :gloss "in five things a father merits for his sons"} {:he "בנוי", :translit "benoy", :gloss "beauty"} {:he "בכח", :translit "be-koach", :gloss "strength"} {:he "בעושר", :translit "be-osher", :gloss "wealth"} {:he "בחכמה", :translit "be-chochmah", :gloss "wisdom"} {:he "בשנים", :translit "be-shanim", :gloss "years"} {:he "יראה על עבדיך פעלך והדרך על בניהם", :translit "yeira'eh al avadecha pe'olacha va-hadracha al baneihem", :gloss "Your work to Your servants, and Your splendor upon their sons"} {:he "גבור בארץ יהיה זרעו דור ישרים יבורך", :translit "gibbor ba-aretz yihyeh zar'o dor yesharim yevorach", :gloss "mighty in the earth shall be his seed; the generation of the upright shall be blessed"} {:he "נער הייתי גם זקנתי ולא ראיתי צדיק נעזב וזרעו מבקש לחם", :translit "na'ar hayiti gam zakannti ve-lo ra'iti tzadik ne'ezav ve-zar'o mevakkeish lachem", :gloss "I was young and also grew old, and I have not seen a righteous one forsaken, nor his seed seeking bread"} {:he "כל היום חונן ומלוה וזרעו לברכה", :translit "kol ha-yom chonen u-malveh ve-zar'o li-vrachah", :gloss "all the day he grants and lends, and his seed is for blessing"} {:he "תחת אבותיך יהיו בניך תשיתמו לשרים בכל הארץ", :translit "tachat avoteicha yihyu banecha tasitemam le-sarim be-chol ha-aretz", :gloss "Instead of your fathers shall be your sons; you shall make them princes in all the earth"} {:he "לא ימושו מפיך ומפי זרעך ומפי זרע זרעך", :translit "lo yamushu mi-picha u-mi-pi zar'echa u-mi-pi zera zar'echa", :gloss "They shall not depart from your mouth, nor from the mouth of your seed, nor from the mouth of your seed's seed"} {:he "למען ירבו ימיכם וימי בניכם על האדמה", :translit "le-ma'an yirbu yemeichem u-yemei baneichem al ha-adamah", :gloss "That your days may be multiplied, and the days of your sons, upon the land"} {:he "יחולו על ראש יואב ואל כל בית אביו", :translit "yeicholu al rosh Yo'av ve-el kol beit aviv", :gloss "May they come upon the head of Joab and upon all his father's house"} {:he "ואל יכרת מבית יואב זב ומצורע ומחזיק בפלך ונופל בחרב וחסר להם", :translit "ve-el yikaret mi-beit Yo'av zav u-metzora u-machazik be-falach ve-nofel be-cherev ve-chaser lahem", :gloss "and may there not be cut off from the house of Joab one with a discharge, and a leper, and one who grasps the distaff, and one who falls by the sword, and one lacking bread"} {:he "זב", :translit "zav", :gloss "one with a discharge"} {:he "ומצורע", :translit "u-metzora", :gloss "and a leper"} {:he "ומחזיק בפלך", :translit "u-machazik be-falach", :gloss "and one who grasps the distaff"} {:he "ונופל בחרב", :translit "ve-nofel be-cherev", :gloss "and one who falls by the sword"} {:he "וחסר להם", :translit "ve-chaser lahem", :gloss "and one lacking bread"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Tagin on the heh of האומן signal five domains in which a father's merit reaches his sons."} {:kind :other, :note "Five blessings — beauty, strength, wealth, wisdom, years — are mapped one-to-one against five curses in Joab's house (2 Samuel 3:29), each curse being the inverse of the corresponding blessing."}], :frame {:text "The heh of האומן carries tagin, which the Ba'al HaTurim reads as marking five domains of intergenerational merit. Each blessing category is anchored in a proof verse: beauty (Psalms 90:16), strength (Psalms 112:2), wealth (Psalms 37:25–26), wisdom (Psalms 45:17 and Isaiah 59:21), and years (Deuteronomy 11:21). The counter-list of five afflictions is drawn from David's curse on Joab's house (2 Samuel 3:29), where each affliction inverts one blessing: discharge drains strength, leprosy destroys beauty, the distaff signifies the unlearned (cf. b. Shabbat 31a where 'grasping the distaff' denotes one unversed in learning), the sword shortens years, and lack of bread negates wealth.", :sources ["Psalms 90:16" "Psalms 112:2" "Psalms 37:25–26" "Psalms 45:17" "Isaiah 59:21" "Deuteronomy 11:21" "2 Samuel 3:29" "b. Shabbat 31a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Tagin on the heh of האומן signal five domains in which a father's merit reaches his sons.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Five blessings — beauty, strength, wealth, wisdom, years — are mapped one-to-one against five curses in Joab's house (2 Samuel 3:29), each curse being the inverse of the corresponding blessing.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:33.093022759Z", :model "glm-5.2"}